{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion` type implements\n`trust_but_verify::graph::Criterion<D>` for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    type Ok: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> NodeId<D>;\n    fn criterion_path(&self) -> CriterionPath;\n    fn version(&self) -> CriterionVersion;\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        ctx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject is a structural requirement. Every criterion type implements `Criterion<D>` for its application domain, with the stated associated type and methods. The marked tests check this by implementing the trait in test criteria and using those criteria through the public validation API.\n\n- **Trait implementations.** The test criteria `Review` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` (`impl[Review/Criterion<Memory>]`), `Review` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs` (`impl[Review/Criterion<Memory>]`) and `Review<O>` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs` (`impl[Review<O>/Criterion<Application>]`) each implement `Criterion<D>` with `type Ok`, `source_node_id`, `criterion_path`, `version` and an async `execute`. A trait declaration with a different shape would not compile against these implementations.\n- **Methods behave as declared.**\n  - `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` asserts the output, `source_node_id`, `criterion_path` and `version` of the returned value.\n  - It also asserts that `execute` runs, and that storage and reload round-trip the `Ok` value through serialization and deserialization.\n  - `caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly` covers `version` and `execute` for a different `Ok` type.\n  - `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` covers `execute` with `Ok = Assessment<Metadata>` and storage in a different domain.\n  - `domain_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk` in `src/authoring/sdk.rs` asserts all three descriptor methods on a real SDK criterion, and also covers `execute` and storage.\n- **Bounds and Send.** `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` uses `Ok = Cell<u32>`, which is `Send` but not `Sync`. It wraps the verify, store, load and refresh futures in a `send(...)` helper, which checks the `Send` bounds on `Ok` and on the execute future at compile time. The `Serialize + DeserializeOwned` bounds on `Ok` are exercised by the store and load round-trips.\n- **Multiple domains.** The trait is implemented for several domains (`Memory`, `Application`, `StoredGraph`, `Project`, `TestDomain`), which matches \"for its application domain\".\n- **Public path.** `public_exports_match_the_appendix` checks that the SDK export inventory matches rustdoc output. That is supporting evidence for the public path `trust_but_verify::graph::Criterion`.\n- **Delegated obligations.** The `answer`, `source_node_id`, `version`, `execute` and `criterion_path` sub-requirements have their own requirements and tests, so this assessment does not re-check their behavior.\n\nI found no plausible violation that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "b8aba858074b87917d741e6bdb62f922585d791a0b517182e03e288af06cf211",
